From b0218dfd30ad0fdb74dba5f580fb0c4953bea270 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:12:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] advisors: the tick's "Show me" places looked up on day
 29 (B3 A1)

On the second month-scan day (29), after the facility, jam and response
scans, advisors.daily predicts the coming tick's announcements and
looks up their places then: AdvisorData.scan.places[id] = [x, z]
([-1, -1]: none found). On the tick an announced advice with a lazy
place and a saved one takes it without a lookup; anything else (no
places: an older save; a record that is not two integers) is looked up
as before. Texts, choices, cooldowns, streak, seen, posts and the issue
list are unchanged.

- announce(): the tick's announcement test (confirm, cooldown x
  2^min(3, streak), quietIf against the news of the 90 days before the
  tick day, ADVICE_PER_MONTH) is one function for monthly() and the
  prediction, so they cannot drift. It calls back for each advice
  before it tests the next, so the tick still takes the same decisions
  in the same order; the prediction also counts the advice it spoke
  for quietIf and duplicates (redundant on the tick: CityState.notify
  always posts, and the cooldown is at least 60 days).
- gather(..., 'predict'): the tick's rules on the saved scans, read
  only (the stall window is written in 'month' mode only), fresh
  places, and no garbage survey (depthRules' Scans.predict: off the
  tick it is a full pass over the homes). recentNews takes the day.
- No prediction without the day-28 zone scan (an older save loaded
  after day 28): gather would scan the zones on day 29 and again on the
  tick.
- AdvisorsSystem.predictPlaces(st) exposes it (tests).

Bit-identical to T2 + P3 on the bot (the 128x15 seed-7 table line for
line) and on both fixtures (cityDigest after 90 days at design
cadence). With P3 under it, dense1m's ticks 10950-11040 waste no
prediction; the prototype on the base wasted playgrounds at d11040
(the ADVICE_PER_MONTH cap: unemployment held only from the tick's
employment sample).

A1 is conditional (B3_DESIGN.md section 8): it ships only if day 29
passes its own timing gate; this commit can be dropped on its own.

tests/sim/advisorsPredict.test.ts: the day-29 place is posted on the
tick without a lookup, [-1, -1] posts none; the prediction is read only
(systemData, news, stats, budget, the random stream; no resident
survey), and empty without a zone scan; saves on day 28 and day 29
post the uninterrupted game's news (text, x, z) on the tick, and a save
without places (or with a corrupt one) looks them up.

